{"uid":"thag2.27","title":"Nandaka (1st)","reference":"Theragāthā 2.27","blocks":[{"kind":"verse","lines":["Though a fine thoroughbred may stumble,","it soon stands firm again.","It gains even more urgency,","and draws its load undeterred.","Even so is one accomplished in vision,","a disciple of the Buddha.","Remember me as a thoroughbred,","the Buddha’s bosom son."]}]}
